  "body": "## Result\n\n2525 / KOU-21.16: **unsolved, 5/5**, with full independent scoped source/proof PASS.\n\nFive genuine turns give inverse-cost and exhaustion obstructions, finite-index and strong-kernel reductions, exact finite-action criteria, conjugacy exclusions, and compatible-product/Baire barriers. The original arbitrary-group separation remains unresolved.\n\n## Essential scope\n\nThe positive set must algebraically generate every group element. Dense generation, a proper invariant semigroup, finite quotient diameters, or a bound for one symmetric generating set do not suffice. Compact/analytic restrictions and finite normal-generation assumptions remain explicit. Bergman and Rosendal are credited; no missing Khelif construction or historical novelty is asserted.\n\nThe additive turn3 control-description clarification is retained prominently. All41 frozen author files and five review files are unchanged. Current README status supersedes only the historical pending-review wording, without editing it.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll311,547 author controls,156 bindings and seven local source hashes replayed; the full independent audit adds6,833 controls and checks all five proofs. Portable replay uses Python's standard library. Optional source verification reports exactly the files supplied.\n\nFresh main and final author ancestry are preserved. Only this target folder and its own QUEUE status/turn cells change. One draft PR, no merge or release, no raw source redistribution.\n",
